        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Household Linen\n\nA large proportion of a family's domestic expenditure was spent on linen. Some fine bed linen was imported from the Netherlands, but plenty was locally made. Wealthy families embellished their linens with embroidery and lace insertions. After childbirth, the cradle and mother's bed were given particularly decorative sheets and pillow covers.\n\nCushion Cover\nEarly 16th century\nItaly\nLinen with silk embroidery and bobbin lace insertions\nV&A: Circ.7-1913\n\n<b>NB: label is incorrect, date should be '1550-1600'. [5 Oct 2006 - 7 Jan 2007]"@en ;
